<Base title="Privacy" description="Vaivoo uses no cookies, no analytics and no third-party scripts. What the web server logs, and your rights.">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p>Vaivoo is a reading site. It does not ask you to sign in, and it does not track you.</p>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No cookies.</li>
    <li>No analytics, advertising or tracking scripts.</li>
    <li>No third-party fonts, embeds or scripts: every page is served from our own server.</li>
    <li>Site search runs in your browser; your search terms are not sent to us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Server logs</h2>
  <p>Like any website, our hosting provider's web server records basic technical data for each request: IP address, time, requested page, browser identification and referring page. These logs are used only to keep the site running and secure, are not combined with other data, and are deleted by the hosting provider on its standard schedule.</p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>If you email us, for example to report a correction, we use your message and address only to handle that request. If your correction is published, we do not name you unless you ask us to.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Under the GDPR you can ask what personal data we hold about you, and ask us to correct or delete it. Contact <a href="mailto:privacy@vaivoo.com">privacy@vaivoo.com</a>. You can also complain to your data protection authority; in Norway that is Datatilsynet.</p>

  <h2>Controller</h2>
  <p>The data controller is the owner of Vaivoo, named on the <a href="/about/">About</a> page.</p>

  <p class="meta">Last updated: 3 October 2026.</p>
</Base>
